{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 16}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   We propose use of a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform\n   an authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about this\n   origin's Service Bindings, i.e. its \"HTTPS\" DNS records.  These\n   instructions can include Encrypted ClientHello (ECH) configurations,\n   allowing the origin to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2023-10-23T19:45:51Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 331216, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/331216/", "rev": "02", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2023-04-21T19:45:51Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing ECHConfigList values.", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about this\n   origin's Service Bindings, i.e. its \"HTTPS\" DNS records.  These\n   instructions can include Encrypted ClientHello (ECH) configurations,\n   allowing the origin, in collaboration with DNS infrastructure\n   elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2024-04-24T19:21:25Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 343890, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/343890/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2023-10-22T19:21:25Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing ECHConfigList values.", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about this\n   origin's Service Bindings, i.e. its \"HTTPS\" DNS records.  These\n   instructions can include Encrypted ClientHello (ECH) configurations,\n   allowing the origin, in collaboration with DNS infrastructure\n   elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2024-01-05T23:03:21Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 335351, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/335351/", "rev": "03", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2023-07-04T23:03:21Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing ECHConfigList values.", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about this\n   origin's Service Bindings, i.e. its \"HTTPS\" DNS records.  These\n   instructions can include Encrypted ClientHello (ECH) configurations,\n   allowing the origin, in collaboration with DNS infrastructure\n   elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2024-04-24T19:21:25Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 360331, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/360331/", "rev": "04", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2024-04-24T07:05:07Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing ECHConfigList values.", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We propose use of a well-known URI at which web servers can publish\n   ECHConfigList values as a way to help get those published in the DNS.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2023-01-26T05:39:19Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 311659, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/311659/", "rev": "00", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2022-07-25T04:39:19Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing ECHConfigList values.", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We propose use of a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform\n   an authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about this\n   origin's Service Bindings, i.e. its \"HTTPS\" DNS records.  These\n   instructions can include Encrypted ClientHello (ECH) configurations,\n   allowing the origin to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2023-04-26T21:37:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 317562, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/317562/", "rev": "01", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2022-10-23T21:37:00Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing ECHConfigList values.", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about its\n   Service Bindings.  The data can include Encrypted ClientHello (ECH)\n   configurations, allowing the origin, in collaboration with DNS\n   infrastructure elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.\n\nNote\n\n   This note is to be removed before publishing as an RFC.\n\n   The source for this draft is in https://github.com/sftcd/wkesni/\n   Issues and PRs are welcome there too.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2025-01-08T22:03:40Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 364597, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/364597/", "rev": "05", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2024-07-07T22:03:40Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing ECHConfigList values.", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about its\n   Service Bindings.  The data can include Encrypted ClientHello (ECH)\n   configurations, allowing the origin, in collaboration with DNS\n   infrastructure elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.\n\nNote\n\n   This note is to be removed before publishing as an RFC.\n\n   The source for this draft is in https://github.com/sftcd/wkesni/\n   Issues and PRs are welcome there too.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2025-10-05T13:50:30Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 389039, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 17, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/389039/", "rev": "07", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2025-04-03T13:50:30Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing service parameters", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about its\n   Service Bindings.  The data can include Encrypted ClientHello (ECH)\n   configurations, allowing the origin, in collaboration with DNS\n   infrastructure elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.\n\nNote\n\n   This note is to be removed before publishing as an RFC.\n\n   The source for this draft is in https://github.com/sftcd/wkesni/\n   Issues and PRs are welcome there too.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2025-04-04T19:12:47Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 372555, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 16, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/372555/", "rev": "06", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2024-10-01T19:12:47Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing service parameters", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about its\n   Service Bindings.  The data can include Encrypted ClientHello (ECH)\n   configurations, allowing the origin, in collaboration with DNS\n   infrastructure elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.\n\nNote\n\n   This note is to be removed before publishing as an RFC.\n\n   The source for this draft is in https://github.com/sftcd/wkesni/\n   Issues and PRs are welcome there too.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2026-01-08T15:44:34Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 395428, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 18, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/395428/", "rev": "08", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2025-07-07T15:44:34Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing service parameters", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about its\n   Service Bindings.  Service binding data can include Encrypted\n   ClientHello (ECH) configurations, that may change frequently.  This\n   allows the origin, in collaboration with DNS infrastructure elements,\n   to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.  Other service bindng data\n   such as information about TLS supported groups is unlikely to change\n   quickly, but the origin is much more likely to have accurate\n   information when changes do occur.  Service data published via this\n   mechanism is typically available via an HTTPS or SVCB resource\n   record.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2026-03-06T13:30:06Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 401101, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 18, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/401101/", "rev": "09", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2025-09-02T13:30:06Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing service parameters", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about its\n   Service Bindings.  Service binding data can include Encrypted\n   ClientHello (ECH) configurations, that may change frequently.  This\n   allows the HTTP origin, in collaboration with DNS infrastructure\n   elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.  Other service\n   binding data such as information about TLS supported groups is\n   unlikely to change quickly, but the HTTP origin is much more likely\n   to have accurate information when changes do occur.  Service data\n   published via this mechanism is typically available via an HTTPS or\n   SVCB resource record.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2026-04-22T21:12:38Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 404333, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 21, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/404333/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2025-10-19T21:12:38Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing service parameters", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about its\n   Service Bindings.  Service binding data can include Encrypted\n   ClientHello (ECH) configurations, that may change frequently.  This\n   allows the HTTP origin, in collaboration with DNS infrastructure\n   elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.  Other service\n   binding data such as information about TLS supported groups is\n   unlikely to change quickly, but the HTTP origin is much more likely\n   to have accurate information when changes do occur.  Service data\n   published via this mechanism is typically available via an HTTPS or\n   SVCB resource record.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2026-05-07T22:11:59Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 407019, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 21, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/407019/", "rev": "11", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2025-11-03T22:11:59Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing service parameters", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about its\n   Service Bindings.  Service binding data can include Encrypted\n   ClientHello (ECH) configurations, that may change frequently.  This\n   allows the HTTP origin, in collaboration with DNS infrastructure\n   elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.  Other service\n   binding data such as information about TLS supported groups is\n   unlikely to change quickly, but the HTTP origin is much more likely\n   to have accurate information when changes do occur.  Service data\n   published via this mechanism is typically available via an HTTPS or\n   SVCB resource record.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2026-05-07T22:11:59Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 407212, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 21, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/407212/", "rev": "11", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/41/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2025-11-04T14:33:35Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing service parameters", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about its\n   Service Bindings.  Service binding data can include Encrypted\n   ClientHello (ECH) configurations, that may change frequently.  This\n   allows the HTTP origin, in collaboration with DNS infrastructure\n   elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.  Other service\n   binding data such as information about TLS supported groups is\n   unlikely to change quickly, but the HTTP origin is much more likely\n   to have accurate information when changes do occur.  Service data\n   published via this mechanism is typically available via an HTTPS or\n   SVCB resource record.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2026-05-07T22:11:59Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 409934, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 21, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/409934/", "rev": "11", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/145/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2025-12-04T14:09:30Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing service parameters", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about its\n   Service Bindings.  Service binding data can include Encrypted\n   ClientHello (ECH) configurations, that may change frequently.  This\n   allows the HTTP origin, in collaboration with DNS infrastructure\n   elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.  Other service\n   binding data such as information about TLS supported groups is\n   unlikely to change quickly, but the HTTP origin is much more likely\n   to have accurate information when changes do occur.  Service data\n   published via this mechanism is typically available via an HTTPS or\n   SVCB resource record.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "expires": "2026-11-04T13:14:44Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 421776, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 21, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/421776/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/145/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2026-05-03T13:14:44Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing service parameters", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}]}